/-!
# Restriction of scalars along an epimorphism of sheaves of rings is fully faithful

Let `α : R ⟶ R'` be an epimorphism in the category of sheaves of (not necessarily commutative)
rings on a site `(C, J)`. This file proves that
`SheafOfModules.restrictScalars α : SheafOfModules R' ⥤ SheafOfModules R` is fully faithful.

The argument is Silver's, carried out directly at the level of sheaves. Given sheaves of
`R'`-modules `G₁` and `G₂` and a morphism `ψ` of their underlying presheaves of abelian groups
which is `R`-linear, the obstruction to its `R'`-linearity is the family
`d s = (x ↦ ψ (s • x) - s • ψ x)`, a section over `X` of the internal hom of the underlying
presheaves of abelian groups. The Leibniz rule `d (s * t) = s • d t + d s • t` says exactly that
`s ↦ [[s, d s], [0, s]]` is a morphism of sheaves of rings from `R'` to the triangular matrix
sheaf of rings `[[R', ℋ], [0, R']]`, where `ℋ` is that internal hom. Since `ψ` is `R`-linear,
this morphism agrees with the diagonal one after composition with `α`, so `Epi α` forces `d = 0`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.sliceSMul`: multiplication by the sections of `R` over `X`
  as a ring homomorphism into the endomorphism ring of the restriction of the underlying
  presheaf of abelian groups of a presheaf of modules to the slice site over `X`.
  `sliceSMulHom` is the same map with its values retyped as morphisms.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.derivSection`: the obstruction `d` above.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.derivSubfunctor`: the sub-bimodule of `ℋ` generated by the
  obstruction, as the range of a map out of a free abelian group on three copies of the sections
  of `R'`; `derivSheaf` is the subsheaf of `ℋ` it generates.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.testSections`, `testSubring`, `testRing`, `testSheaf`: the
  triangular matrix sheaf of rings `[[R', 𝒩], [0, R']]`, as the subring of the trivial square-zero
  extension of the sections of `R'` by the sections of `ℋ` whose off-diagonal entry lies in `𝒩`,
  with `restrHom` and `restrSub` its restriction maps.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.diagHom`, `twistHom`: the two morphisms of sheaves of
  rings `R' ⟶ T` that the epimorphism `α` is tested against.

## Main results

* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.restrictScalars_fullyFaithful_of_epi`: restriction of
  scalars along an epimorphism of sheaves of not necessarily commutative rings is fully
  faithful. This is the noncommutative variant of [Stacks, Tag 0930]; Stacks' statement, for an
  epimorphism of sheaves of commutative rings, is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restrictScalars_fullyFaithful_of_epi`. `full_restrictScalars_of_epi` is the fullness half.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.derivSection_mul`: the Leibniz rule, and
  `derivSection_eq_zero_of_epi`: the vanishing of the obstruction.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.isSheaf_forget_of_isSheaf`: the underlying presheaf of
  types of a sheaf of rings is a sheaf, with no size condition relating the universe of the rings
  to the universes of the site.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.isSheaf_of_bijective_pair`: a presheaf of types whose
  sections are, naturally and bijectively, pairs of sections of two sheaves is a sheaf.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.small_sheafify_obj`: **a subfunctor with small sections
  generates a subsheaf with small sections**, the bound being the size of the site and in
  particular independent of the universe of the sections of the ambient presheaf.
* `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.isSheaf_testRing`: the triangular test presheaf of rings
  is a sheaf.

## Implementation notes

**Universes.** The site is `C : Type u'` with `Category.{v'} C`, the sheaves of rings are
`RingCat.{u}`-valued and the module universe is `v`. The internal hom `ℋ` is valued in
`Type (max u' v' v)`, while the test object must be a sheaf of rings in `RingCat.{u}`. The test
object is therefore built from the subsheaf `derivSheaf` generated by the obstruction, whose
sections are bounded by the size of the site; the hypotheses `[Small.{u} C]` and
`[LocallySmall.{u} C]` make that bound `Type u` (`small_sheafify_obj`, `small_derivSheaf_obj`).
The module universe `v` is unconstrained.

**The internal hom is taken in abelian groups.** For a noncommutative `R'` the group of
`R`-linear morphisms `G₁|_X ⟶ G₂|_X` is not an `R'`-bimodule, and `d s` does not lie in it. The
group of morphisms of the underlying presheaves of abelian groups is an `R'`-bimodule by pre- and
post-composition, and `d s` lies in it.

**Instances keyed on `presheafHom`.** Instance search does not unfold `presheafHom`, which is a
plain `def`, so the abelian group and the four module structures on its sections are declared as
instances at the spelling `(presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X`; each is the
corresponding instance of the group of natural transformations, so no new structure is created
and no diamond arises. For the same reason `sliceSMulHom` is a `def` with an ascribed type: at
the spelling `End F` the additive and multiplicative structures `rw`, `simp` and `abel` see are
those of the endomorphism ring, and `Preadditive.add_comp` then fails to fire.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0930](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0930)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04VN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04VN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08YS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08YS)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite Limits

namespace Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver

universe w₁ w₂ w₃ v v' u u'

/-- The free ring on one generator corepresents the forgetful functor of `RingCat.{u}`. -/
noncomputable def forgetRingCatCoyonedaIso :
    coyoneda.obj (op (RingCat.of (FreeRing PUnit.{u + 1}))) ≅ forget RingCat.{u} :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun R ↦ Equiv.toIso
    { toFun := fun φ ↦ φ.hom (FreeRing.of PUnit.unit)
      invFun := fun r ↦ RingCat.ofHom (FreeRing.lift (fun _ ↦ r))
      left_inv := fun φ ↦ RingCat.hom_ext (FreeRing.hom_ext (fun _ ↦ by simp))
      right_inv := fun r ↦ by simp }) (fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- The underlying presheaf of types of a sheaf of rings is a sheaf, with no size condition
relating the universe of the rings to the universes of the site. -/
theorem isSheaf_forget_of_isSheaf {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    (P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}) (h : Presheaf.IsSheaf J P) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J (P ⋙ forget RingCat.{u}) := by
  rw [CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type]
  exact Presieve.isSheaf_iso J (Functor.isoWhiskerLeft P forgetRingCatCoyonedaIso)
    (h (RingCat.of (FreeRing PUnit.{u + 1})))

section PairSheaf

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- A presheaf of types carrying two restriction-compatible families of maps to sheaves of types,
jointly bijective at every object, is itself a sheaf. -/
theorem isSheaf_of_bijective_pair {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w₁} {Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w₂} {T : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w₃}
    (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf J P) (hQ : Presheaf.IsSheaf J Q)
    (p : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, T.obj X → P.obj X) (q : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, T.obj X → Q.obj X)
    (hp : ∀ {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (t : T.obj X), p Y (T.map f t) = P.map f (p X t))
    (hq : ∀ {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (t : T.obj X), q Y (T.map f t) = Q.map f (q X t))
    (hbij : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Function.Bijective (fun t : T.obj X ↦ (p X t, q X t))) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J T := by
  have hP' := (CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J P).1 hP
  have hQ' := (CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J Q).1 hQ
  rw [CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type]
  intro X S hS x hx
  have hxP : Presieve.FamilyOfElements.Compatible (P := P)
      (fun ⦃Y⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X) (hf : S.arrows f) ↦ p (op Y) (x f hf)) := by
    intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm
    rw [← hp, ← hp]
    exact congrArg (p (op Z)) (hx g₁ g₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm)
  have hxQ : Presieve.FamilyOfElements.Compatible (P := Q)
      (fun ⦃Y⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X) (hf : S.arrows f) ↦ q (op Y) (x f hf)) := by
    intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm
    rw [← hq, ← hq]
    exact congrArg (q (op Z)) (hx g₁ g₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm)
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := (hbij (op X)).2
    ((hP' S hS).amalgamate _ hxP, (hQ' S hS).amalgamate _ hxQ)
  have htp : p (op X) t = (hP' S hS).amalgamate _ hxP := congrArg Prod.fst ht
  have htq : q (op X) t = (hQ' S hS).amalgamate _ hxQ := congrArg Prod.snd ht
  have hamal : ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X) (hf : S.arrows f), T.map f.op t = x f hf := by
    intro Y f hf
    have h₁ : p (op Y) (T.map f.op t) = p (op Y) (x f hf) := by
      rw [hp, htp]; exact (hP' S hS).valid_glue hxP f hf
    have h₂ : q (op Y) (T.map f.op t) = q (op Y) (x f hf) := by
      rw [hq, htq]; exact (hQ' S hS).valid_glue hxQ f hf
    refine (hbij (op Y)).1 ?_
    change (p (op Y) (T.map f.op t), q (op Y) (T.map f.op t)) =
      (p (op Y) (x f hf), q (op Y) (x f hf))
    rw [h₁, h₂]
  refine ⟨t, hamal, fun t' ht' ↦ ?_⟩
  have h₁ : p (op X) t' = p (op X) t :=
    (hP' S hS).isSeparatedFor.ext fun Y f hf ↦ by
      rw [← hp, ← hp, ht' f hf, hamal f hf]
  have h₂ : q (op X) t' = q (op X) t :=
    (hQ' S hS).isSeparatedFor.ext fun Y f hf ↦ by
      rw [← hq, ← hq, ht' f hf, hamal f hf]
  refine (hbij (op X)).1 ?_
  change (p (op X) t', q (op X) t') = (p (op X) t, q (op X) t)
  rw [h₁, h₂]

end PairSheaf

section SliceAction

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}

/-- Multiplication by the sections of `R` over `X`, as a ring homomorphism to the endomorphism
ring of the restriction to the slice site over `X` of the underlying presheaf of abelian groups
of a presheaf of `R`-modules `M`. The component at an object `W` of the slice site is
multiplication by the restriction of the section to `W`. -/
noncomputable def sliceSMul (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    R.obj X →+* End ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M.presheaf) where
  toFun s := End.of
    { app := fun W ↦ ((M.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul (R.map W.unop.hom.op s)).asHom
      naturality := fun W W' φ ↦ by
        have hc : W.unop.hom.op ≫ (Over.forget X.unop).op.map φ = W'.unop.hom.op :=
          Quiver.Hom.unop_inj (Over.w φ.unop)
        have h : R.map ((Over.forget X.unop).op.map φ) (R.map W.unop.hom.op s) =
            R.map W'.unop.hom.op s := by
          rw [← CategoryTheory.comp_apply, ← R.map_comp, hc]
        have key := PresheafOfModules.smul_map (M := M) ((Over.forget X.unop).op.map φ)
          (R.map W.unop.hom.op s)
        rw [h] at key
        exact key.symm }
  map_one' := End.ext <| NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦
    congrArg End.asHom (map_one ((M.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul.comp (R.map W.unop.hom.op).hom)))
  map_mul' s t := End.ext <| NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦
    congrArg End.asHom (map_mul ((M.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul.comp (R.map W.unop.hom.op).hom) s t))
  map_zero' := End.ext <| NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦
    congrArg End.asHom (map_zero ((M.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul.comp (R.map W.unop.hom.op).hom)))
  map_add' s t := End.ext <| NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦
    congrArg End.asHom (map_add ((M.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul.comp (R.map W.unop.hom.op).hom) s t))

/-- The slice action `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver.sliceSMul`, read as a morphism rather
than as an element of the endomorphism ring. -/
noncomputable def sliceSMulHom (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X) :
    ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M.presheaf) ⟶ ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M.presheaf) :=
  (sliceSMul M X s).asHom

/-- The component of `sliceSMulHom M X s` at `W` is multiplication by the restriction of `s`
to `W`. -/
theorem sliceSMulHom_app (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X)
    (W : (Over X.unop)ᵒᵖ) :
    (sliceSMulHom M X s).app W = ((M.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul (R.map W.unop.hom.op s)).asHom :=
  rfl

/-- `sliceSMulHom M X 1` is the identity. -/
theorem sliceSMulHom_one (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    sliceSMulHom M X 1 = 𝟙 _ := congrArg End.asHom (map_one (sliceSMul M X))

/-- `sliceSMulHom M X 0` is zero. -/
theorem sliceSMulHom_zero (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    sliceSMulHom M X 0 = 0 := congrArg End.asHom (map_zero (sliceSMul M X))

/-- `sliceSMulHom M X` is additive. -/
theorem sliceSMulHom_add (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s t : R.obj X) :
    sliceSMulHom M X (s + t) = sliceSMulHom M X s + sliceSMulHom M X t :=
  congrArg End.asHom (map_add (sliceSMul M X) s t)

/-- `sliceSMulHom M X` sends a product `s * t` to the composite of the actions of `t` and
of `s`. -/
theorem sliceSMulHom_mul (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s t : R.obj X) :
    sliceSMulHom M X (s * t) = sliceSMulHom M X t ≫ sliceSMulHom M X s :=
  congrArg End.asHom (map_mul (sliceSMul M X) s t)

/-- A difference `a ≫ b - b ≫ c` of two composites with a common term `b` is unchanged when
`a` and `c` are replaced by equal morphisms. -/
theorem sub_comp_congr {A B : AddCommGrpCat.{v}} {a a' : A ⟶ A} {c c' : B ⟶ B} {b : A ⟶ B}
    (ha : a = a') (hc : c = c') : a ≫ b - b ≫ c = a' ≫ b - b ≫ c' := by rw [ha, hc]

end SliceAction

/-! ### The internal hom as a bimodule over the sections of the ring -/

section HomBimodule

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ)

/-- The sections over `X` of the internal hom of the underlying presheaves of abelian groups form
an abelian group: they are the morphisms of a preadditive category. -/
noncomputable instance instAddCommGroupPresheafHomObj :
    AddCommGroup ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup
    ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₁.presheaf ⟶ (Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₂.presheaf))

/-- Post-composition makes the sections over `X` of the internal hom a module over the
endomorphism ring of the restriction of `M₂`. -/
noncomputable instance instModuleEndPresheafHomObj :
    Module (End ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₂.presheaf))
      ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module (End ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₂.presheaf))
    ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₁.presheaf ⟶ (Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₂.presheaf))

/-- Pre-composition makes the sections over `X` of the internal hom a right module over the
endomorphism ring of the restriction of `M₁`. -/
noncomputable instance instModuleEndOpPresheafHomObj :
    Module (End ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₁.presheaf))ᵐᵒᵖ
      ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module (End ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₁.presheaf))ᵐᵒᵖ
    ((Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₁.presheaf ⟶ (Over.forget X.unop).op ⋙ M₂.presheaf))

/-- Scaling a section of the internal hom on the left by a section of `R`: multiply the value by
the section. -/
noncomputable instance instModulePresheafHomObj :
    Module (R.obj X) ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :=
  Module.compHom _ (sliceSMul M₂ X)

/-- Scaling a section of the internal hom on the right by a section of `R`: multiply the argument
by the section. -/
noncomputable instance instModuleOpPresheafHomObj :
    Module (R.obj X)ᵐᵒᵖ ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :=
  Module.compHom _ (RingHom.op (sliceSMul M₁ X))

/-- The left and right actions of the sections of `R` on the internal hom commute: one is
post-composition and the other pre-composition. -/
instance instSMulCommClassPresheafHomObj :
    SMulCommClass (R.obj X) (R.obj X)ᵐᵒᵖ
      ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :=
  ⟨fun a b η ↦ Category.assoc (sliceSMul M₁ X b.unop).asHom η (sliceSMul M₂ X a).asHom⟩

end HomBimodule

/-! ### The restriction maps of the internal hom are semilinear -/

section HomRestriction

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R)

/-- Restricting the zero section of the internal hom gives zero. -/
theorem map_zero_presheafHomObj {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f 0 = 0 :=
  NatTrans.ext (funext fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- The restriction maps of the internal hom are additive. -/
theorem map_add_presheafHomObj {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (η ζ : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f (η + ζ) =
      (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f η +
        (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f ζ :=
  NatTrans.ext (funext fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- The restriction to `W` of the restriction along `f` of a section of `R` over `X`. -/
private theorem map_hom_op {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (s : R.obj X) (W : (Over Y.unop)ᵒᵖ) :
    R.map ((Over.map f.unop).obj W.unop).hom.op s = R.map W.unop.hom.op (R.map f s) := by
  have hc : f ≫ W.unop.hom.op = ((Over.map f.unop).obj W.unop).hom.op :=
    Quiver.Hom.unop_inj rfl
  rw [← CategoryTheory.comp_apply, ← R.map_comp, hc]

/-- The restriction maps of the internal hom are semilinear for the left action: restricting
`s • η` gives the restriction of `s` acting on the restriction of `η`. -/
theorem map_smul_presheafHomObj {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (s : R.obj X)
    (η : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f (s • η) =
      R.map f s • (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f η :=
  NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦ congrArg
    (fun r ↦ η.app ((Over.map f.unop).op.obj W) ≫ ((M₂.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul r).asHom)
    (map_hom_op f s W))

/-- The restriction maps of the internal hom are semilinear for the right action. -/
theorem map_op_smul_presheafHomObj {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (s : R.obj X)
    (η : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f (MulOpposite.op s • η) =
      MulOpposite.op (R.map f s) • (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f η :=
  NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦ congrArg
    (fun r ↦ ((M₁.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul r).asHom ≫ η.app ((Over.map f.unop).op.obj W))
    (map_hom_op f s W))

end HomRestriction

/-! ### The triangular test presheaf of rings -/

section TestRing

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R)

/-- The sections over `X` of the triangular test ring: pairs `(s, η)` consisting of a section of
`R` and a section of the internal hom, multiplied as the two-by-two triangular matrices
`[[s, η], [0, s]]`. -/
noncomputable abbrev testSections (X : Cᵒᵖ) : Type (max u u' v' v) :=
  TrivSqZeroExt (R.obj X) ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X)

/-- The restriction maps of the triangular test ring: restrict both entries. -/
noncomputable def restrHom {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    testSections M₁ M₂ X →+* testSections M₁ M₂ Y where
  toFun x := (R.map f x.fst, (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f x.snd)
  map_one' := TrivSqZeroExt.ext (map_one (R.map f).hom) (map_zero_presheafHomObj M₁ M₂ f)
  map_zero' := TrivSqZeroExt.ext (map_zero (R.map f).hom) (map_zero_presheafHomObj M₁ M₂ f)
  map_add' x y := TrivSqZeroExt.ext (map_add (R.map f).hom x.fst y.fst)
    (map_add_presheafHomObj M₁ M₂ f x.snd y.snd)
  map_mul' x y := TrivSqZeroExt.ext (map_mul (R.map f).hom x.fst y.fst) (by
    change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f
      (x.fst • y.snd + MulOpposite.op y.fst • x.snd) = _
    rw [map_add_presheafHomObj, map_smul_presheafHomObj, map_op_smul_presheafHomObj]
    rfl)

/-- The first entry of a restricted section of the triangular test ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrHom_fst {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : testSections M₁ M₂ X) :
    (restrHom M₁ M₂ f x).fst = R.map f x.fst := rfl

/-- The second entry of a restricted section of the triangular test ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrHom_snd {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : testSections M₁ M₂ X) :
    (restrHom M₁ M₂ f x).snd = (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f x.snd := rfl

/-- Restriction along the identity is the identity. -/
theorem restrHom_id (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : testSections M₁ M₂ X) : restrHom M₁ M₂ (𝟙 X) x = x :=
  TrivSqZeroExt.ext
    (by rw [restrHom_fst, R.map_id]; rfl)
    (by rw [restrHom_snd]
        exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map_id X) x.snd)

/-- Restriction along a composite is the composite of the restrictions. -/
theorem restrHom_comp {X Y Z : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z) (x : testSections M₁ M₂ X) :
    restrHom M₁ M₂ (f ≫ g) x = restrHom M₁ M₂ g (restrHom M₁ M₂ f x) :=
  TrivSqZeroExt.ext
    (by rw [restrHom_fst, restrHom_fst, restrHom_fst, R.map_comp]; rfl)
    (by rw [restrHom_snd, restrHom_snd, restrHom_snd]
        exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
          ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map_comp f g) x.snd)

end TestRing

/-! ### The derivation attached to a morphism of the underlying presheaves of abelian groups -/

section Deriv

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (ψ : M₁.presheaf ⟶ M₂.presheaf)

/-- The obstruction to `R`-linearity of a morphism `ψ` of the underlying presheaves of abelian
groups: the section of the internal hom over `X` attached to a section `s` of `R` over `X` whose
value at a section `x` is `ψ (s • x) - s • ψ x`. -/
noncomputable def derivSection (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X :=
  sliceSMulHom M₁ X s ≫ Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget X.unop).op ψ -
    Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget X.unop).op ψ ≫ sliceSMulHom M₂ X s

/-- The obstruction vanishes at `1`. -/
theorem derivSection_one (X : Cᵒᵖ) : derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X 1 = 0 := by
  simp only [derivSection, sliceSMulHom_one, Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id, sub_self]
  rfl

/-- The obstruction vanishes at `0`. -/
theorem derivSection_zero (X : Cᵒᵖ) : derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X 0 = 0 := by
  simp only [derivSection, sliceSMulHom_zero, Limits.zero_comp, Limits.comp_zero, sub_self]
  rfl

/-- The obstruction is additive. -/
theorem derivSection_add (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s t : R.obj X) :
    derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X (s + t) =
      derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s + derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X t := by
  simp only [derivSection, sliceSMulHom_add, Preadditive.add_comp, Preadditive.comp_add]
  abel

/-- The Leibniz rule: the obstruction is a derivation into the internal hom, the two actions
being the left and right actions of the triangular test ring. -/
theorem derivSection_mul (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s t : R.obj X) :
    derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X (s * t) =
      s • derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X t + MulOpposite.op t • derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s := by
  change _ = derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X t ≫ sliceSMulHom M₂ X s +
    sliceSMulHom M₁ X t ≫ derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s
  simp only [derivSection, sliceSMulHom_mul, Preadditive.sub_comp, Preadditive.comp_sub,
    Category.assoc]
  abel

/-- The obstruction is compatible with the restriction maps. -/
theorem map_derivSection {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (s : R.obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f (derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s) =
      derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ Y (R.map f s) :=
  NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦ sub_comp_congr
    (congrArg (fun r ↦ ((M₁.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul r).asHom) (map_hom_op f s W))
    (congrArg (fun r ↦ ((M₂.obj (op W.unop.left)).smul r).asHom) (map_hom_op f s W)))

/-- If the obstruction vanishes at a section `s`, then `ψ` commutes with multiplication by `s`
on the sections over `X`. -/
theorem app_smul_of_derivSection_eq_zero (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X)
    (h : derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s = 0) (m : M₁.obj X) :
    ψ.app X (s • m) = s • ψ.app X m := by
  have hr : R.map (𝟙 X) s = s := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (R.map_id X) s
  have h₁ : sliceSMulHom M₁ X s ≫ Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget X.unop).op ψ =
      Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget X.unop).op ψ ≫ sliceSMulHom M₂ X s := by
    rw [← sub_eq_zero]; exact h
  have h₂ := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (congrFun (congrArg NatTrans.app h₁) (op (Over.mk (𝟙 X.unop)))) m
  change ψ.app X (R.map (𝟙 X) s • m) = R.map (𝟙 X) s • ψ.app X m at h₂
  rwa [hr] at h₂

end Deriv

/-! ### A sheafified subfunctor with small sections has small sections -/

section Smallness

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w₁}

/-- **A subfunctor with small sections generates a subsheaf with small sections.** The bound is
the size of the site: no condition relates it to the universe `w₁` of the sections of the
ambient presheaf. -/
theorem small_sheafify_obj (G : Subfunctor F) (hF : Presieve.IsSeparated J F)
    [∀ Y : Cᵒᵖ, Small.{w₂} (G.obj Y)] [Small.{w₂} C] [LocallySmall.{w₂} C] (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Small.{w₂} ((G.sheafify J).obj X) := by
  refine small_of_injective (f := fun s : ((G.sheafify J).obj X) ↦
    (fun (Y : C) (f : Y ⟶ X.unop) ↦ {x : G.obj (op Y) | x.1 = F.map f.op s.1})) ?_
  intro s s' h
  refine Subtype.ext ((hF _ s.2).ext fun Y f hf ↦ ?_)
  have h₂ : ({x : G.obj (op Y) | x.1 = F.map f.op s.1} : Set _) =
      {x : G.obj (op Y) | x.1 = F.map f.op s'.1} := congrFun (congrFun h Y) f
  have h₃ : (⟨F.map f.op s.1, hf⟩ : G.obj (op Y)) ∈
      ({x : G.obj (op Y) | x.1 = F.map f.op s'.1} : Set _) := by
    rw [← h₂]; rfl
  exact h₃

end Smallness


/-! ### The sub-bimodule of the internal hom generated by the obstruction -/

section DerivSubfunctor

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (ψ : M₁.presheaf ⟶ M₂.presheaf)

/-- The restriction maps of the internal hom, as additive maps. -/
noncomputable def mapAddHom {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X →+
      (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj Y where
  toFun η := (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map i η
  map_zero' := map_zero_presheafHomObj M₁ M₂ i
  map_add' := map_add_presheafHomObj M₁ M₂ i

/-- A generator of the sub-bimodule: the obstruction at a section, scaled on both sides. -/
noncomputable def gen (X : Cᵒᵖ) (τ : R.obj X × R.obj X × R.obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X :=
  τ.1 • (MulOpposite.op τ.2.2 • derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X τ.2.1)

/-- The sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction, as the range of a map from a free abelian
group on three copies of the sections of `R`. -/
noncomputable def genHom (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    FreeAbelianGroup (R.obj X × R.obj X × R.obj X) →+
      (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X :=
  FreeAbelianGroup.lift (gen M₁ M₂ ψ X)

/-- Restricting a triple of sections of `R`. -/
noncomputable def restrTriple {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y)
    (τ : R.obj X × R.obj X × R.obj X) : R.obj Y × R.obj Y × R.obj Y :=
  (R.map i τ.1, R.map i τ.2.1, R.map i τ.2.2)

/-- Restricting a generator of the sub-bimodule gives the generator at the restricted triple. -/
theorem mapAddHom_gen {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y) (τ : R.obj X × R.obj X × R.obj X) :
    mapAddHom M₁ M₂ i (gen M₁ M₂ ψ X τ) = gen M₁ M₂ ψ Y (restrTriple i τ) := by
  change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map i
      (τ.1 • (MulOpposite.op τ.2.2 • derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X τ.2.1)) = _
  rw [map_smul_presheafHomObj, map_op_smul_presheafHomObj, map_derivSection]
  rfl

/-- An additive map of sections of the internal hom sends the range of `genHom` at `X` into the
range of `genHom` at `Y` as soon as it sends each generator there. -/
private theorem map_mem_range_genHom {X Y : Cᵒᵖ}
    (φ : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X →+
      (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj Y)
    (hφ : ∀ τ, φ (gen M₁ M₂ ψ X τ) ∈ Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ Y))
    {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X} (hz : z ∈ Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ X)) :
    φ z ∈ Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ Y) := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hz
  induction x using FreeAbelianGroup.induction_on with
  | zero => exact ⟨0, by simp⟩
  | of τ => simpa only [genHom, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of] using hφ τ
  | neg τ h =>
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := h
      exact ⟨-y, by rw [map_neg, hy, map_neg, map_neg]⟩
  | add x y hx hy =>
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hx
      obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hy
      exact ⟨a + b, by rw [map_add, ha, hb, map_add, map_add]⟩

/-- The range of `genHom` is stable under the restriction maps of the internal hom. -/
theorem mapAddHom_mem_range {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y)
    (z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X)
    (hz : z ∈ Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ X)) :
    mapAddHom M₁ M₂ i z ∈ Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ Y) :=
  map_mem_range_genHom M₁ M₂ ψ (mapAddHom M₁ M₂ i) (fun τ ↦
    ⟨FreeAbelianGroup.of (restrTriple i τ), by
      rw [genHom, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of]
      exact (mapAddHom_gen M₁ M₂ ψ i τ).symm⟩) hz

/-- **The sub-bimodule of the internal hom generated by the obstruction.** -/
noncomputable def derivSubfunctor : Subfunctor (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf) where
  obj X := Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ X)
  map i _ hz := mapAddHom_mem_range M₁ M₂ ψ i _ hz

/-- The sections of the sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction are `u`-small. -/
theorem small_derivSubfunctor_obj (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Small.{u} ((derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Small.{u} (Set.range (genHom M₁ M₂ ψ X)))

/-- The obstruction lies in the sub-bimodule it generates. -/
theorem derivSection_mem_derivSubfunctor (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X) :
    derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X := by
  refine ⟨FreeAbelianGroup.of (1, s, 1), ?_⟩
  rw [genHom, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, gen, MulOpposite.op_one, one_smul, one_smul]


/-- `0` lies in the sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction. -/
theorem zero_mem_derivSubfunctor (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (0 : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X :=
  ⟨0, map_zero _⟩

/-- The sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction is closed under addition. -/
theorem add_mem_derivSubfunctor {X : Cᵒᵖ} {z z' : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X}
    (hz : z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X) (hz' : z' ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X) :
    z + z' ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hz
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hz'
  exact ⟨x + y, map_add _ _ _⟩

/-- The sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction is closed under negation. -/
theorem neg_mem_derivSubfunctor {X : Cᵒᵖ} {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X}
    (hz : z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X) :
    -z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hz
  exact ⟨-x, map_neg _ _⟩

/-- The sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction is closed under the left action. -/
theorem smul_mem_derivSubfunctor {X : Cᵒᵖ} (a : R.obj X)
    {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X}
    (hz : z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X) :
    a • z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X :=
  map_mem_range_genHom M₁ M₂ ψ (DistribSMul.toAddMonoidHom
    ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) a) (fun τ ↦
    ⟨FreeAbelianGroup.of (a * τ.1, τ.2.1, τ.2.2), by
      rw [genHom, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of]
      exact mul_smul a τ.1 (MulOpposite.op τ.2.2 • derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X τ.2.1)⟩) hz

/-- The sub-bimodule generated by the obstruction is closed under the right action. -/
theorem op_smul_mem_derivSubfunctor {X : Cᵒᵖ} (b : R.obj X)
    {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X}
    (hz : z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X) :
    MulOpposite.op b • z ∈ (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj X :=
  map_mem_range_genHom M₁ M₂ ψ (DistribSMul.toAddMonoidHom
    ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) (MulOpposite.op b)) (fun τ ↦
    ⟨FreeAbelianGroup.of (τ.1, τ.2.1, τ.2.2 * b), by
      rw [genHom, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of]
      simp only [gen, DistribSMul.toAddMonoidHom_apply]
      rw [← smul_comm τ.1 (MulOpposite.op b), MulOpposite.op_mul, mul_smul]⟩) hz

end DerivSubfunctor


/-! ### The subsheaf generated by the obstruction -/

section DerivSheaf

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (ψ : M₁.presheaf ⟶ M₂.presheaf)
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- The restriction maps of the internal hom commute with negation. -/
theorem map_neg_presheafHomObj {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y)
    (η : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) :
    (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map i (-η) =
      -((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map i η) :=
  map_neg (mapAddHom M₁ M₂ i) η

/-- **The subsheaf of the internal hom generated by the obstruction.** -/
noncomputable def derivSheaf : Subfunctor (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf) :=
  (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).sheafify J

/-- `0` lies in the subsheaf generated by the obstruction. -/
theorem zero_mem_derivSheaf (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (0 : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X) ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X := by
  refine J.superset_covering (fun Y f _ ↦ ?_) (J.top_mem X.unop)
  change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f.op 0 ∈ _
  rw [map_zero_presheafHomObj]
  exact zero_mem_derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ _

/-- The subsheaf generated by the obstruction is closed under addition. -/
theorem add_mem_derivSheaf {X : Cᵒᵖ} {z z' : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X}
    (hz : z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) (hz' : z' ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) :
    z + z' ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X := by
  refine J.superset_covering (fun Y f hf ↦ ?_) (J.intersection_covering hz hz')
  change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f.op (z + z') ∈ _
  rw [map_add_presheafHomObj]
  exact add_mem_derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ hf.1 hf.2

/-- The subsheaf generated by the obstruction is closed under negation. -/
theorem neg_mem_derivSheaf {X : Cᵒᵖ} {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X}
    (hz : z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) : -z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X := by
  refine J.superset_covering (fun Y f hf ↦ ?_) hz
  change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f.op (-z) ∈ _
  rw [map_neg_presheafHomObj]
  exact neg_mem_derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ hf

/-- The subsheaf generated by the obstruction is closed under the left action. -/
theorem smul_mem_derivSheaf {X : Cᵒᵖ} (a : R.obj X)
    {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X} (hz : z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) :
    a • z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X := by
  refine J.superset_covering (fun Y f hf ↦ ?_) hz
  change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f.op (a • z) ∈ _
  rw [map_smul_presheafHomObj]
  exact smul_mem_derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ _ hf

/-- The subsheaf generated by the obstruction is closed under the right action. -/
theorem op_smul_mem_derivSheaf {X : Cᵒᵖ} (b : R.obj X)
    {z : (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X} (hz : z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) :
    MulOpposite.op b • z ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X := by
  refine J.superset_covering (fun Y f hf ↦ ?_) hz
  change (presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).map f.op (MulOpposite.op b • z) ∈ _
  rw [map_op_smul_presheafHomObj]
  exact op_smul_mem_derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ _ hf

/-- The obstruction lies in the subsheaf it generates. -/
theorem derivSection_mem_derivSheaf (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X) :
    derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X :=
  (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).le_sheafify J _ (derivSection_mem_derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ X s)

/-- The subsheaf generated by the obstruction is a sheaf when `M₂` is. -/
theorem isSheaf_derivSheaf (hM₂ : Presheaf.IsSheaf J M₂.presheaf) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).toFunctor := by
  rw [CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type]
  exact (derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).sheafify_isSheaf
    ((CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).1 (hM₂.hom M₁.presheaf))

/-- The sections of the subsheaf generated by the obstruction are `u`-small when the site is
small relative to `u`. -/
theorem small_derivSheaf_obj (hM₂ : Presheaf.IsSheaf J M₂.presheaf)
    [Small.{u} C] [LocallySmall.{u} C] (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Small.{u} ((derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) := by
  have : ∀ Y : Cᵒᵖ, Small.{u} ((derivSubfunctor M₁ M₂ ψ).obj Y) :=
    small_derivSubfunctor_obj M₁ M₂ ψ
  exact small_sheafify_obj J _
    (((CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).1 (hM₂.hom M₁.presheaf)).isSeparated) X

end DerivSheaf


/-! ### The triangular test sheaf of rings -/

section TestSubring

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (ψ : M₁.presheaf ⟶ M₂.presheaf)
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- **The sections of the triangular test ring.** The subring of the full triangular ring whose
off-diagonal entry lies in the subsheaf generated by the obstruction. -/
noncomputable def testSubring (X : Cᵒᵖ) : Subring (testSections M₁ M₂ X) where
  carrier := {x | x.snd ∈ (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X}
  zero_mem' := zero_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J X
  one_mem' := zero_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J X
  add_mem' hx hy := add_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J hx hy
  neg_mem' hx := neg_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J hx
  mul_mem' hx hy := add_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J
    (smul_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J _ hy) (op_smul_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J _ hx)

/-- The sections of the triangular test ring over `X` are the pairs consisting of a section of
`R` and a section of the subsheaf generated by the obstruction. -/
def testPairEquiv (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X ≃ R.obj X × ((derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X) where
  toFun x := (x.1.fst, ⟨x.1.snd, x.2⟩)
  invFun y := ⟨(y.1, y.2.1), y.2.2⟩
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv _ := rfl

variable [∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Small.{u} ((derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X)]

/-- The sections of the triangular test ring are `u`-small. -/
instance smallTestSubring (X : Cᵒᵖ) : Small.{u} (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X) :=
  small_of_injective (testPairEquiv M₁ M₂ ψ J X).injective

/-- The restriction maps of the triangular test ring. -/
noncomputable def restrSub {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y) :
    testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X →+* testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J Y where
  toFun x := ⟨restrHom M₁ M₂ i x.1, (derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).map i x.2⟩
  map_one' := Subtype.ext (map_one (restrHom M₁ M₂ i))
  map_mul' x y := Subtype.ext (map_mul (restrHom M₁ M₂ i) x.1 y.1)
  map_zero' := Subtype.ext (map_zero (restrHom M₁ M₂ i))
  map_add' x y := Subtype.ext (map_add (restrHom M₁ M₂ i) x.1 y.1)

/-- **The triangular test presheaf of rings**, valued in the universe of the sections of `R`. -/
noncomputable def testRing : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} where
  obj X := RingCat.of (Shrink.{u} (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X))
  map i := RingCat.ofHom
    ((Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J _)).symm.toRingHom.comp
      ((restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J i).comp (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J _)).toRingHom))
  map_id X := RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x ↦ by
    change (Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm (restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J (𝟙 X) (Shrink.ringEquiv _ x)) = x
    rw [show restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J (𝟙 X) (Shrink.ringEquiv _ x) = Shrink.ringEquiv _ x from
      Subtype.ext (restrHom_id M₁ M₂ X _)]
    exact (Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm_apply_apply x)
  map_comp i j := RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x ↦ by
    change (Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm (restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J (i ≫ j) (Shrink.ringEquiv _ x)) =
      (Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm (restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J j (Shrink.ringEquiv _
        ((Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm (restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J i (Shrink.ringEquiv _ x)))))
    rw [(Shrink.ringEquiv _).apply_symm_apply]
    exact congrArg _ (Subtype.ext (restrHom_comp M₁ M₂ i j _)))

/-- The restriction maps of `testRing` are those of `testSubring`, transported along `Shrink`. -/
theorem testRing_map_symm {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y) (x : testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X) :
    (testRing M₁ M₂ ψ J).map i ((Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm x) =
      (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J Y)).symm (restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J i x) := by
  change (Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm (restrSub M₁ M₂ ψ J i (Shrink.ringEquiv _
    ((Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm x))) = _
  rw [(Shrink.ringEquiv _).apply_symm_apply]

end TestSubring


/-! ### The ring homomorphisms tested against the epimorphism -/

section TestHoms

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
  (M₁ M₂ : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (ψ : M₁.presheaf ⟶ M₂.presheaf)
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- The twisted ring homomorphism `s ↦ [[s, d s], [0, s]]` into the triangular test ring. -/
noncomputable def twistRingHom (X : Cᵒᵖ) : R.obj X →+* testSections M₁ M₂ X where
  toFun s := (s, derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s)
  map_one' := TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl (derivSection_one M₁ M₂ ψ X)
  map_zero' := TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl (derivSection_zero M₁ M₂ ψ X)
  map_add' s t := TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl (derivSection_add M₁ M₂ ψ X s t)
  map_mul' s t := TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl (derivSection_mul M₁ M₂ ψ X s t)

variable [∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Small.{u} ((derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J).obj X)]

/-- The diagonal morphism of presheaves of rings `R ⟶ T`, `s ↦ [[s, 0], [0, s]]`. -/
noncomputable def diagHom : R ⟶ testRing M₁ M₂ ψ J where
  app X := RingCat.ofHom
    ((Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm.toRingHom.comp
      ((TrivSqZeroExt.inlHom (R.obj X) ((presheafHom M₁.presheaf M₂.presheaf).obj X)).codRestrict
        (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X) fun _ ↦ zero_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J X))
  naturality X Y i := RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun s ↦ by
    change (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J Y)).symm
        ⟨TrivSqZeroExt.inl (R.map i s), _⟩ =
      (testRing M₁ M₂ ψ J).map i ((Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm
        ⟨TrivSqZeroExt.inl s, _⟩)
    rw [testRing_map_symm]
    exact congrArg _ (Subtype.ext (TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl
      (map_zero_presheafHomObj M₁ M₂ i))))

/-- The twisted morphism of presheaves of rings `R ⟶ T`, `s ↦ [[s, d s], [0, s]]`. -/
noncomputable def twistHom : R ⟶ testRing M₁ M₂ ψ J where
  app X := RingCat.ofHom
    ((Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm.toRingHom.comp
      ((twistRingHom M₁ M₂ ψ X).codRestrict (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)
        fun s ↦ derivSection_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J X s))
  naturality X Y i := RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun s ↦ by
    change (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J Y)).symm
        ⟨(R.map i s, derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ Y (R.map i s)), _⟩ =
      (testRing M₁ M₂ ψ J).map i ((Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm
        ⟨(s, derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s), _⟩)
    rw [testRing_map_symm]
    exact congrArg _ (Subtype.ext (TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl
      (map_derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ i s).symm)))

/-- The value of `diagHom` at a section `s` is the diagonal element `[[s, 0], [0, s]]`. -/
theorem diagHom_app_apply (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X) :
    (diagHom M₁ M₂ ψ J).app X s = (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm
      ⟨TrivSqZeroExt.inl s, zero_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J X⟩ := rfl

/-- The value of `twistHom` at a section `s` is `[[s, d s], [0, s]]`. -/
theorem twistHom_app_apply (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R.obj X) :
    (twistHom M₁ M₂ ψ J).app X s = (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring M₁ M₂ ψ J X)).symm
      ⟨(s, derivSection M₁ M₂ ψ X s), derivSection_mem_derivSheaf M₁ M₂ ψ J X s⟩ := rfl

end TestHoms


/-! ### Stacks 0930 with the site-only universe hypothesis -/

section Main

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {R R' : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} [Small.{u} C] [LocallySmall.{u} C]
  (G₁ G₂ : SheafOfModules.{v} R') (ψ : G₁.val.presheaf ⟶ G₂.val.presheaf)

/-- The sections of the subsheaf generated by the obstruction are `u`-small. -/
instance smallDerivSheafObj (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Small.{u} ((derivSheaf G₁.val G₂.val ψ J).obj X) :=
  small_derivSheaf_obj G₁.val G₂.val ψ J G₂.isSheaf X

/-- The triangular test presheaf of rings is a sheaf. -/
theorem isSheaf_testRing : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (testRing G₁.val G₂.val ψ J) := by
  refine Presheaf.isSheaf_ringCat_of_isSheaf_forget _ ?_
  have key : ∀ {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (i : X ⟶ Y) (t : (testRing G₁.val G₂.val ψ J).obj X),
      testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J Y
          (Shrink.ringEquiv _ ((testRing G₁.val G₂.val ψ J).map i t)) =
        (R'.obj.map i (testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X (Shrink.ringEquiv _ t)).1,
          (derivSheaf G₁.val G₂.val ψ J).toFunctor.map i
            (testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X (Shrink.ringEquiv _ t)).2) := by
    intro X Y i t
    change testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J Y (Shrink.ringEquiv _
      ((Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm
        (restrSub G₁.val G₂.val ψ J i (Shrink.ringEquiv _ t)))) = _
    rw [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    rfl
  exact isSheaf_of_bijective_pair (isSheaf_forget_of_isSheaf R'.obj R'.property)
    (isSheaf_derivSheaf G₁.val G₂.val ψ J G₂.isSheaf)
    (fun X t ↦ (testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X (Shrink.ringEquiv _ t)).1)
    (fun X t ↦ (testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X (Shrink.ringEquiv _ t)).2)
    (fun i t ↦ congrArg Prod.fst (key i t)) (fun i t ↦ congrArg Prod.snd (key i t))
    (fun X ↦ (testPairEquiv G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X).bijective.comp
      (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X)).bijective)

/-- The triangular test sheaf of rings. -/
noncomputable def testSheaf : Sheaf J RingCat.{u} :=
  ⟨testRing G₁.val G₂.val ψ J, isSheaf_testRing G₁ G₂ ψ⟩

variable (α : R ⟶ R')
  (hψ : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (r : R.obj.obj X) (m : G₁.val.obj X),
    ψ.app X (α.hom.app X r • m) = α.hom.app X r • ψ.app X m)

omit [Small.{u} C] [LocallySmall.{u} C] in
include hψ in
/-- If `ψ` is `R`-linear, the obstruction vanishes on sections coming from `R`. -/
theorem derivSection_app_eq_zero (X : Cᵒᵖ) (r : R.obj.obj X) :
    derivSection G₁.val G₂.val ψ X (α.hom.app X r) = 0 := by
  have key : sliceSMulHom G₁.val X (α.hom.app X r) ≫
        Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget X.unop).op ψ =
      Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget X.unop).op ψ ≫
        sliceSMulHom G₂.val X (α.hom.app X r) := by
    refine NatTrans.ext (funext fun W ↦ ?_)
    have hnat : R'.obj.map W.unop.hom.op (α.hom.app X r) =
        α.hom.app (op W.unop.left) (R.obj.map W.unop.hom.op r) := by
      rw [← CategoryTheory.comp_apply, ← CategoryTheory.comp_apply, α.hom.naturality]
    change (sliceSMulHom G₁.val X (α.hom.app X r)).app W ≫ ψ.app (op W.unop.left) =
      ψ.app (op W.unop.left) ≫ (sliceSMulHom G₂.val X (α.hom.app X r)).app W
    rw [sliceSMulHom_app, sliceSMulHom_app, hnat]
    exact AddCommGrpCat.ext fun m ↦ hψ (op W.unop.left) (R.obj.map W.unop.hom.op r) m
  simp only [derivSection, key, sub_self]
  rfl

include hψ in
/-- If `α` is an epimorphism and `ψ` is `R`-linear, the obstruction vanishes for every section
of `R'`. -/
theorem derivSection_eq_zero_of_epi [Epi α] (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : R'.obj.obj X) :
    derivSection G₁.val G₂.val ψ X s = 0 := by
  have hsheaf : (ObjectProperty.homMk (twistHom G₁.val G₂.val ψ J) :
        R' ⟶ testSheaf G₁ G₂ ψ) = ObjectProperty.homMk (diagHom G₁.val G₂.val ψ J) := by
    rw [← cancel_epi α]
    refine Sheaf.hom_ext (NatTrans.ext (funext fun Z ↦ RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun r ↦ ?_)))
    change (twistHom G₁.val G₂.val ψ J).app Z (α.hom.app Z r) =
      (diagHom G₁.val G₂.val ψ J).app Z (α.hom.app Z r)
    rw [twistHom_app_apply, diagHom_app_apply]
    exact congrArg _ (Subtype.ext (TrivSqZeroExt.ext rfl
      (derivSection_app_eq_zero G₁ G₂ ψ α hψ Z r)))
  have h : twistHom G₁.val G₂.val ψ J = diagHom G₁.val G₂.val ψ J := Sheaf.hom_ext_iff.mp hsheaf
  have h₂ : (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X)).symm
        ⟨(s, derivSection G₁.val G₂.val ψ X s),
          derivSection_mem_derivSheaf G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X s⟩ =
      (Shrink.ringEquiv (testSubring G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X)).symm
        ⟨TrivSqZeroExt.inl s, zero_mem_derivSheaf G₁.val G₂.val ψ J X⟩ := by
    rw [← twistHom_app_apply, ← diagHom_app_apply, h]
  exact congrArg TrivSqZeroExt.snd
    (congrArg Subtype.val ((Shrink.ringEquiv _).symm.injective h₂))

end Main

section Conclusion

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {R R' : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} [Small.{u} C] [LocallySmall.{u} C] (α : R ⟶ R')

/-- Restriction of scalars along an epimorphism of sheaves of rings is full. -/
theorem full_restrictScalars_of_epi [Epi α] :
    (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{v} α).Full where
  map_surjective {G₁ G₂} g := by
    refine ⟨⟨PresheafOfModules.homMk ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map g.val) ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · intro X r m
      refine app_smul_of_derivSection_eq_zero G₁.val G₂.val _ X r ?_ m
      refine derivSection_eq_zero_of_epi G₁ G₂ _ α (fun Y r' m' ↦ ?_) X r
      exact (g.val.app Y).hom.map_smul r' m'
    · exact SheafOfModules.hom_ext (PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun _ ↦
        ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun _ ↦ rfl))

/-- Restriction of scalars along an epimorphism `α : R ⟶ R'` of sheaves of not necessarily
commutative rings on a site is fully faithful. Equivalently, for any two sheaves of `R'`-modules
every morphism of their restrictions to `R` is uniquely `R'`-linear. The site is assumed small
relative to the universe of the sections of the rings (`Small.{u} C`, `LocallySmall.{u} C`).

This is the noncommutative variant of [Stacks, Tag 0930]: the epimorphism is asked for in the
category of sheaves of rings, `Sheaf J RingCat`. Stacks' own statement, where the rings are
commutative and the epimorphism is one of sheaves of commutative rings, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restrictScalars_fullyFaithful_of_epi`. -/
theorem restrictScalars_fullyFaithful_of_epi [Epi α] :
    Nonempty (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{v} α).FullyFaithful :=
  have := full_restrictScalars_of_epi.{v} α
  ⟨.ofFullyFaithful _⟩

end Conclusion

end Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Silver

end
